  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">Mitiga&#xe7;&#xe3;o e Estabiliza&#xe7;&#xe3;o de Conflitos</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Government Bolsters Mozambican Justice Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="PT">Reduzir a amea&#xe7;a ou o impacto dos conflitos violentos e promover a resolu&#xe7;&#xe3;o pac&#xed;fica das diferen&#xe7;as, mitigar a viol&#xea;ncia caso esta j&#xe1; tenha eclodido ou estabelecer um quadro para a paz e a reconcilia&#xe7;&#xe3;o. Isto &#xe9; feito atrav&#xe9;s da identifica&#xe7;&#xe3;o das causas do conflito e do fracasso do Estado; apoiar respostas precoces que abordem as causas e consequ&#xea;ncias da instabilidade e do conflito; e desenvolver solu&#xe7;&#xf5;es duradouras para os problemas que geram conflitos. Isto inclui apoio a processos e mecanismos de reconcilia&#xe7;&#xe3;o e mitiga&#xe7;&#xe3;o de conflitos, independentemente da origem do conflito, embora isto possa exigir a integra&#xe7;&#xe3;o com outros elementos.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through a direct grant of $2.2 million, JUSTA will provide in-service training to an estimated 70 judges and 110 prosecutors to prosecute wildlife trafficking crimes, protect human rights, and combat corruption in the northern provinces of Cabo Delgado, Nampula, and Niassa. Given the challenges of access to justice in remote areas, JUSTA will support the use of mobile courts, enabling judges to reach citizens where they live and protect their rights. To enhance efficiency, JUSTA will help the Supreme Court and the Attorney Generals Office implement an automated case management tracking system. JUSTA will also support the fight against corruption by strengthening internal audit offices and judicial inspections.</narrative>
  </description>
